  "drawnOn": "B722",
  "description": "Pan Am's last scheme, applied from 1984: the cheatline gone and the white body carrying 'PAN AM' in huge blue capitals across the cabin windows, from just behind the forward door to over the wing. A light grey lower fuselage under a level line well below the windows, a small black nose tip, the big blue globe on the white fin and bare metal engines. The A300s and A310s were delivered in it; the 727s and 747s were repainted into it from 1984 on, so both it and the cheatline were common in 1985.",
