  "notes": "Measured 2026-11-24 for ghost flights on 727-200 N550PS (May 1985, fitted to shapes/B722.json), with the A300B4 and the 747 as types (B744-passenger stands in for the 747-100, -200 and SP). The grey's top is a level line at -0.70 m. The lettering is Pan Am's own and no typeface comes close: it's named as a wordmark (PA1927/wordmark) with stand-ins that only get its width and weight. Colors are from faded slides.",
  "types": {
    "B722": {
      "note": "On the 727 the globe is about 2.9 m across and centered at the top of the centre engine's S-duct intake, its lower half on the intake fairing, and the US flag is on that fairing ahead of the fin (N550PS, N4740). Both are in the fin's space carried down below its root, where a renderer draws fin logos over an S-duct's fairing. On other types the scheme's own globe is centered on the fin and the flag is left out.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "sourceRefs": [
